            <ArticleTitle>Single coronary artery complicating stent implantation for homograft stenosis in tetralogy of Fallot.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>405-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Successful stent implantation for conduit stenosis has been described; however, this procedure may be complicated by compression of adjacent structures during expansion. We report on a rare case of a single right coronary artery system complicating stent implantation for relief of homograft stenosis in tetralogy of Fallot.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
